sections.say:
"This is hash-group-then-sort: one Map keyed by the natural grouping field (date), values are arrays in input order. Emit by sorting keys.

```
const byDate = new Map();
for (const r of records) {
  if (!byDate.has(r.date)) byDate.set(r.date, []);   // lazy bucket init
  byDate.get(r.date).push(`${r.provider}: ${r.note}`);
}
return [...byDate.keys()].sort().map(d => `${d} — ${byDate.get(d).join('; ')}`);
```

"Three load-bearing pieces. (1) Map (not Object) — preserves insertion order, accepts non-string keys if dates were ever Dates, and `.has`/`.get`/`.set` semantics are clearer than `hasOwnProperty` dances. (2) Lazy init — `if (!has) set([])` before the push, otherwise the first `.get(...).push` on a new date throws on `undefined.push`. (3) ISO-string sort — `YYYY-MM-DD` is lexicographically chronological because every component is fixed-width and the most-significant comes first. No Date parsing needed."

